When the pixels of a 2D canvas can’t be allocated, Ladybird creates no
context for it in the Compositor, so the canvas draws nothing. Blink’s
CanvasRenderingContextHost::IsValidImageSize() refuses a canvas wider
or taller than 65535 pixels, or over its maximum area, and such a
canvas gets no buffer. WebKit’s CanvasBase::validateArea() refuses a
canvas over its maximum area, and a canvas whose ImageBuffer can’t be
created draws nothing. And when a canvas is over Gecko’s size limits,
CanvasRenderingContext2D::EnsureTarget() puts it in an error state with
SetErrorState(), so it draws to a shared error target.
